<title>ITALY: Italy has global trade surplus in December.</title>
<headline>Italy has global trade surplus in December.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italy had a 3.591 trillion lire global trade surplus in December, the Italian Exchange Office said in a statement.</p>
<p> ITALIAN TRADE BALANCE  Dec 96	  Nov 96	  Dec 95</p>
<p> Amount (lire)	    +3.591 trln  +3.622 trln    +2.210 trln</p>
<p> Cumulative yr to date +41.929 trln +38.769 trln   +22.943 trln</p>
<p>Note: The calculation is based on flows through the financial sector on transactions in excess of 20 million lire.</p>
</text>
